The diff does both parts of #1045:

• `/doctor` project-context row: files the directory fence refuses are now listed as refused instead of disappearing. It reuses the existing formatter from /context (refused_context_file_line), which cleans the reason text before display. When every file is refused, the row warns and names them instead of telling you to "create YOYO.md or run /init".
• Shell `yoyo doctor`: it now builds the same fence a real session would, through cli::startup_dir_restrictions. That function was pulled out of parse_permission_and_dir_config, so both places use one construction and nothing re-parses the toml. Before, shell doctor passed an empty fence.

